DAY 1 — QUICK START
Small steps. Stronger every day.

WHAT IS INCLUDED
• Existing nutrition dashboard, food library, food history and settings.
• Workouts: Bench press, squat and deadlift days, six exercises each.
• Focus lift progress: latest top set, personal best and dated session results.
• Separate weight (kg) and reps for every set, previous results, notes and date.
• Automatic workout drafts and saved session history. Blank sets are skipped.
• Cardio: activity, minutes, calories burned, optional distance and notes.
• Cardio history with edit/delete and today’s calories/minutes totals.
• Dark navy background, orange sunrise/1 logo and matching phone icons.
• Offline cache for app files after the first successful online load.

1. OPEN IN VS CODE
Extract this ZIP first. Open the Day1 folder in VS Code (File > Open Folder).
The folder you open should contain index.html alongside css, js and icons.
Use your Live Server extension to open index.html. No terminal commands,
build process, package installation or account keys are needed.
Do not open the ZIP itself or double-click index.html to test storage/offline.

2. UPDATE YOUR EXISTING GITHUB PROJECT
Back up your current project before replacing files.
Copy EVERYTHING INSIDE the Day1 folder into the root of your existing
Day 1 GitHub repository, replacing matching files. Include the new workouts.html,
cardio.html and new JavaScript files. Keep your existing repository metadata.
Do not nest the Day1 folder inside the website root: index.html should stay
in the same location as your original index.html.
Commit and push the updated files to the branch already serving your site.
Keep your current GitHub Pages repository/address to retain the same browser
storage origin. Your GitHub repository does not need to be renamed to Day 1.
If you use GitHub’s web upload, upload the extracted files/folders, NOT this ZIP.

3. CHECK THE LIVE APP
After the updated site is available, open its usual address while online.
Close and reopen the app after the first visit so its new offline cache is active.
Check Today/Food, Workouts, Cardio, History and Settings.
Log a small test session, reopen the app and check it remains in history.
To update a stale home-screen name/icon, remove the old shortcut and add
Day 1 again from Safari’s Share menu. Check your existing data before doing so.
Do not clear website data to refresh the icon.

4. LOG A WORKOUT
Choose Workout 1, 2 or 3 and a date. Enter kg and reps separately for each set.
Use 0 kg for an unweighted movement. For dumbbells, enter weight per dumbbell;
for barbells, enter the total bar weight. Be consistent when comparing sessions.
Drafts are saved per training day as you type. Choose that day again to resume.
Finish workout saves to history, clears that draft and updates lift progress.
The top set is the heaviest set, with more reps breaking ties.
Previously saved bench press, squat and deadlift sets count automatically.
Any older Push, Pull or Legs draft is available in the workout selector.
You can save an incomplete session by leaving unused sets completely blank.
Each started set needs both weight and reps. Delete test sessions in history.
Workouts are not calorie estimates. Cardio is tracked separately.

5. LOG CARDIO
Choose activity and date, then enter minutes and calories from your watch or
machine. Calories are manual records, not app-generated estimates. Optional
fields: distance in kilometres and notes. Use 0 calories if unknown.
Finish logging with Save cardio. Edit or delete entries in Activity history.
Cardio calories do not automatically increase your food calorie target.

DATA AND LIMITATIONS
Data stays in this device/browser using local storage. GitHub hosts the app’s
files; it does not store or sync your personal food/workout/cardio records.
Another phone, computer, browser or Live Server address has separate data.
The original macroTrack_* nutrition keys are preserved so the existing browser
can continue using its saved data at the same website address. Do not clear
browser/site data or use private browsing for records you want to keep.
Habits beyond workouts/nutrition/cardio are not included in this release.

